  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Q28MZOLZab0mgYdNB+yJjjMqp7k=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:18.095Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The failure\n\n```tsx\n// \u2705 bundles in Next, Vite or anything else, with no alias or stub\nimport { GraphQLReactorProvider } from \"@powerhousedao/reactor-browser/graphql-client\";\n\n// \u274c drags a Postgres driver and node built-ins into a browser bundle\nimport { GraphQLReactorProvider } from \"@powerhousedao/reactor-browser\";\n```\n\nThe package root re-exports the whole package, and part of that **value-imports** `@powerhousedao/reactor`, whose single entry reaches `pg` (`dns`/`fs`/`net`/`tls`), `@electric-sql/pglite` and `node:worker_threads`. None of it runs on the light-client path, but a browser bundler still has to resolve it \u2014 and Turbopack fails on `node:worker_threads` before any app code runs.\n\n## Why the subpath is safe\n\nThe `/graphql-client` entry imports the reactor **for types only**. Types are erased at compile time, so a bundler never sees them. The few runtime values the client actually needs are mirrored inside `reactor-browser`, with compile-time assertions that fail if they ever drift from the reactor's own definitions.\n\nThe built entry imports exactly `react`, `document-model`, `graphql`, `graphql-request`, `graphql-tag`, `graphql-ws/client`, `@powerhousedao/shared/document-model`, `@powerhousedao/shared/document-drive`, `change-case`, `remeda` and `slug` \u2014 no database driver, no node built-ins. A test walks the entry's import graph and fails if that regresses.\n\n## The general shape\n\nThis is a recurring class of failure, not a one-off: a package whose root entry serves both server and browser consumers will pull server-only backends into a browser bundle, and the fix is always to import the browser subpath. `@powerhousedao/reactor-attachments/client` is the same pattern. The monorepo's `test/test-fusion/` app is a worked example \u2014 it imports the subpath and has no bundler configuration at all.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/08-ReactorBrowserClient/01-OverviewAndQuickstart.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:33:17.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:18.095Z"
    }
  },
